    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "84728d99_30fc50f1",
        "filename": "third_party/libgrapheme/BUILD.gn",
        "patchSetId": 38
      },
      "lineNbr": 12,
      "author": {
        "id": 5140
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-07-31T18:07:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m guessing that libgrapheme must normally build with `-freestanding` just to ensure that it doesn\u0027t use any on the standard library? That\u0027s fine as far as it goes, but it would get in the way of some things. It\u0027s probably better to build it in Skia without `-freestanding` unless it requires that (it invokes undefined behavior by re-using names that would be defined in the standard library).",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 12,
        "startChar": 19,
        "endLine": 12,
        "endChar": 33
      },
      "revId": "393990e454b81d6d73f80bc1797fd3dbbbe1f6e2",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e911ff04_80dfffed",
        "filename": "third_party/libgrapheme/BUILD.gn",
        "patchSetId": 38
      },
      "lineNbr": 49,
      "author": {
        "id": 5140
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-07-31T18:07:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It\u0027s a good idea for the developers on libgrapheme to use these, but since this isn\u0027t directly our code (code we work on) there isn\u0027t really any benefit to having these warnings in our build. We also don\u0027t `-Werror` for `third_party` in general for similar reasons.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 49,
        "startChar": 54,
        "endLine": 49,
        "endChar": 86
      },
      "revId": "393990e454b81d6d73f80bc1797fd3dbbbe1f6e2",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
